Small thing about how this test fails: without the fix, `assert.throws` throws inside the listen callback, so `server.close(done)` never runs and mocha hangs until the timeout instead of reporting a clean failure. That's what I hit when I ran it against master with `lib/application.js` reverted. Wrapping it in `try`/`finally` would make a regression show up as a normal failure:

```js
var server = app.listen(0, function () {
  try {
    assert.throws(function () {
      server.emit('error', new Error('post-listen boom'))
    }, /post-listen boom/)
  } finally {
    server.close(done)
  }
})
```

